# `market::State`

The market a strip is priced in: spot, interest rate and dividend yield.

All three are `Series`. Each must have one element or the same number of elements as the instrument's strikes and maturities, so one field prices a strip in one market, or a set of scenarios (a vector of spots against a single option, a rate curve against several maturities). Rates and yields are annual and continuously compounded and may be negative. [`market::make`](market_make.md) builds a one-element state from numbers.

## Fields

### `spot`

`pluss::Series`, default `undefined`.

The underlying price(s), positive; one element or one per option.

### `rate`

`pluss::Series`, default `undefined`.

Annual continuously compounded risk-free rate(s); may be negative.

### `dividend_yield`

`pluss::Series`, default `undefined`.

Annual continuous dividend yield(s); may be negative.

## Guidance

Member `Field::market`.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1

The spot. One option under five spots: the payoff curve as scenarios.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace mod = fin::module;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  mod::Field field{.instrument = fin::instrument::make(fin::pricing::Call, 100.0, 1.0),
                   .market = {.spot = pluss::series::linspace(80.0, 120.0, 5, pluss::ScalarType::Float64), .rate = pluss::make_series({0.05}), .dividend_yield = pluss::make_series({0.0})},
                   .model = fin::model::make(fin::model::Kind::BlackScholes, {0.2}), .controls = {.engine = mod::Engine::Analytic, .risk = mod::Risk::PriceOnly}};
  out.writeln("spots :", field.market.spot.items<double>());
  out.writeln("prices:", field.price().price.items<double>());
}
```

### Example 2

The rate. Four rates for one option: a call is worth more at higher rates.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace mod = fin::module;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  mod::Field field{.instrument = fin::instrument::make(fin::pricing::Call, 100.0, 1.0),
                   .market = {.spot = pluss::make_series({100.0}), .rate = pluss::make_series({-0.01, 0.0, 0.03, 0.06}), .dividend_yield = pluss::make_series({0.0})},
                   .model = fin::model::make(fin::model::Kind::BlackScholes, {0.2}), .controls = {.engine = mod::Engine::Analytic, .risk = mod::Risk::PriceOnly}};
  out.writeln("rates :", field.market.rate.items<double>());
  out.writeln("prices:", field.price().price.items<double>());
}
```

### Example 3

The dividend yield. A higher yield lowers a call.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace mod = fin::module;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  mod::Field field{.instrument = fin::instrument::make(fin::pricing::Call, 100.0, 1.0),
                   .market = {.spot = pluss::make_series({100.0}), .rate = pluss::make_series({0.05}), .dividend_yield = pluss::make_series({0.0, 0.02, 0.05})},
                   .model = fin::model::make(fin::model::Kind::BlackScholes, {0.2}), .controls = {.engine = mod::Engine::Analytic, .risk = mod::Risk::PriceOnly}};
  out.writeln("yields:", field.market.dividend_yield.items<double>());
  out.writeln("prices:", field.price().price.items<double>());
}
```

### Example 4

Mismatched lengths are refused: two spots and three rates cannot be paired.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

#include <string>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace mod = fin::module;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  mod::Field field{.instrument = fin::instrument::make(fin::pricing::Call, 100.0, 1.0),
                   .market = {.spot = pluss::make_series({100.0, 101.0}), .rate = pluss::make_series({0.01, 0.02, 0.03}), .dividend_yield = pluss::make_series({0.0})},
                   .model = fin::model::make(fin::model::Kind::BlackScholes, {0.2}), .controls = {.engine = mod::Engine::Analytic}};
  try {
    (void)(field.price());
  } catch (const std::exception &e) {
    const std::string text(e.what());
    out.writeln(text.substr(0, text.find('\n')));
  }
}
```

